# latticedeform

- Label: Lattice Deform
- Category: Copernicus (`Cop`), Houdini 22.0.368
- Inputs: 0 to 2
- Parameters: 45 (exact, read from Houdini by hython)
- Used by the height graph: no

## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/latticedeform.html
- Summary (EN): The Lattice Deform node applies grid-based deformation to a layer, where the grid points act as handles that reshape the image. It offers finer deformation than the Bend COP, which is better suited to quick simple warps.
- Résumé (FR) : Déforme une couche à l'aide d'une grille de points de contrôle, avec plus de finesse que le nœud Bend pour des déformations simples.

- Inputs meaning: ["size_ref: representative layer that sets the output image size and controls its metadata", "source: the source layer to deform"]

- Key parameters: ["Signature: layer type the source accepts", "Filter: method used to sample the image", "Mode: Linear (deformation follows the grid exactly) or Smooth (NURBS interpolation for fluid deformation)", "U / V: point density in each direction when NURBS curves convert to polygons", "Cells per Column / Columns: grid cell and column counts, always differing by one", "Row 0: number of grid points in a row, set through the row tabs", "Point 0_0: image-space position of a grid point, shown as a viewport handle"]

- Caveats: ["Columns and Cells per Column are linked: changing one changes the other by one", "The Handles tool moves grid points directly in the viewport", "U and V affect the output only when Smooth mode converts NURBS to polygons", "For simple quick deformations the Bend COP is recommended", "Page targets Houdini 22.0 and notes availability since 21.0; the Filter options are described in the Copernicus glossary, not on this page"]

